## LEAD 2: Desktop Windows key-storage ACL bypass → identity + DB compromise

**Source:** bigpickle, laguna, ling3, nemotron3 | **Confidence:** 95 | **Class:** MISCONFIG
**Asset:** `github.com/threema-ch/threema-desktop` — `apps/desktop/src/common/node/{fs.ts,key-storage/index.ts,electron-main.ts}`

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 In scope? | ✅ Yes — "Desktop 2.x App Source Code (github.com/threema-ch/threema-desktop)" is In-scope |
| Q2 Reachable? | ⚠️ Local — requires same-user process on the victim's Windows machine |
| Q3 Real impact? | ✅ Yes — co-located malware extracts permanent Ed25519 private key + SQLite message-DB key WITHOUT the master password |
| Q4 GET/HEAD proof? | ✅ RAG-verified (source code read). Live PoC requires Windows host |
| Q5 Novel? | ✅ Yes — no prior report |
| Q6 Not rejected? | ✅ Yes — real local credential theft, not just best-practice gap |
| Q7 Triager accept? | ✅ Yes (accepted by 4/5 models) |

**Verdict: VALID** (with note: requires local/same-user access on Windows)

**Minimal proof (RAG-verified):**
- `fs.ts:41` — `fileModeInternalObjectIfPosix()` returns `{}` on `win32`
- `key-storage/index.ts:559-561` — `_writeOrOverrideFile()` spreads `{}` → `fsPromises.writeFile()` → no ACL on `keystorage.bin`
- `electron-main.ts:944-945` — `keystorage.password.bin` written via `safeStorage.encryptString()` (DPAPI) with same `{}` options → no ACL
- Inner layer exposes `identityData.ck` (32-byte Ed25519 private key) + `databaseKey` (SQLCipher key)
- Any same-user process: `CryptUnprotectData` → master password → Argon2id → XSalsa20-Poly1305 decrypt → identity + DB key

**Impact:** Local attacker/malware exfiltrates the victim's permanent Threema identity (private key) + message-database encryption key → offline decrypt of entire local message store WITHOUT the master password.

**CVSS 3.1:** `AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N` — **7.1 (Medium-High)**. High confidentiality + integrity impact but requires local access. String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N`

**Report to:** Threema security channel.

