      • databaseKey = 32-byte SQLCipher key (used raw, no re-KDF)

  STEP 4_identity_key_extraction
    Artifact: Ed25519 private key (ck)
    Src:      inner/v3.ts:65 — IdentityData.ck
    Method:   Parse protobuf field → 32-byte seed
    This is the permanent, offline-capable identity signing key.  An attacker can forge sender auth on behalf of the victim.

  STEP 5_database_decrypt
    Files: threema.sqlite
    Src:   db/sqlite.ts:220 — PRAGMA key = databaseKey (raw, no PBKDF2)
    Method: sqlcipher3 threema.sqlite "PRAGMA key = x'…'"
    The databaseKey from step 3 is used directly as the SQLCipher key with no additional derivation.  `PRAGMA cipher_page_size=4096; PRAGMA kdf_iter=64; PRAGMA key=x'...';` unlocks the entire message store offline.

